  "goodToKnow": "Die Abtreibung is abortion; the neutral medical and legal term is der Schwangerschaftsabbruch. In Germany, § 218 of the criminal code formally makes it unlawful but exempts it from punishment within the first 12 weeks if the woman has had counselling (Beratungsregelung) and a three-day waiting period. In 2022 the ban on doctors providing information (§ 219a) was abolished. Whether to legalise it further remains debated. Plural: die Abtreibungen."
